Vercel Web Analytics Installation for Next.js

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the SeniorEase Next.js project.

## Changes Implemented:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Added 415 packages as dependencies

### 2. Modified Files
- **app/layout.tsx**: Added Analytics component integration
  - Imported Analytics from '@vercel/analytics/next'
  - Added <Analytics /> component inside the <body> tag after the LanguageProviderWrapper
  - Preserved all existing code structure and functionality

- **package.json**: Updated dependencies to include @vercel/analytics

- **package-lock.json**: Updated with new dependency tree

## Implementation Details:
- Project uses App Router architecture (app directory)
- TypeScript-based layout file
- Analytics component placed at the end of the body tag, after the children content
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices

## Verification:
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ All dependencies installed correctly
- ✅ No existing functionality disrupted
- ✅ TypeScript types properly imported

## Notes:
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals
- Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard once deployed
- No additional configuration needed for basic analytics tracking
- The ESLint configuration in the project has a pre-existing issue unrelated to these changes
